cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Apollo: a Discontinuous Galerkin solver for hyperbolic PDEs on unstructured grids"
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sousa
    given-names: Eder
repository-code: "https://github.com/emarinhoss/apollo"
abstract: >-
  Apollo is a high-order Discontinuous Galerkin finite element solver for
  hyperbolic partial differential equations on unstructured grids, built on
  PETSc and MPI. It implements Maxwell's equations, the compressible Euler
  equations, multifluid plasma models and scalar advection, and is used for
  nuclear fusion device modelling (field-reversed configurations, rotating
  magnetic field heating), computational electromagnetics and compressible
  fluid dynamics.
keywords:
  - discontinuous Galerkin
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - plasma physics
  - nuclear fusion
  - computational electromagnetics
  - unstructured mesh
  - PETSc
  - high-performance computing
license: MIT
